      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While iron supplements can help alleviate symptoms of iron deficiency, taking extremely high doses like 200mg/day is not recommended. The recommended daily dose of ferrous sulfate for adults is typically 18mg (about 100mg after splitting it into 2 servings, 50mg per dose). Taking high doses without consulting a doctor or iron deficiency monitor can cause gastrointestinal side effects, interact with medications, or even trigger iron overload. Before starting supplements, it's essential to consult a healthcare professional to determine the best course of action for your specific needs.",
